[38;5;231m⏺[39m Task 3 (topWords) isn't done yet: the review found a bug and the fix is still running in the background.

  The bug is that a typographic apostrophe in a word isn't treated as the same character as a straight one.
  [38;5;153mtopWords("keeper’s keeper's", 5)[39m should return one entry, [38;5;153mkeeper's[39m with count 2, but it returns two entries with count
  1 each. The line meant to convert [38;5;153m’[39m to [38;5;153m'[39m has a straight apostrophe in its pattern, so it changes nothing. The test
  for this rule types both words with straight apostrophes, so it passed anyway.

  I've sent this to a fresh implementer as fix round 1 of 5. It will change the test to use a real typographic
  apostrophe, confirm the test fails, then fix the pattern. A narrower re-review of just that fix follows.

  The reviewer's three minor points are logged for the final review:
  - One test copies the whole stop-word list instead of checking only the stop words that appear in the sample passage.
  - Some test names start with "D1:" or "D2:" labels instead of describing the behaviour.
  - The implementer's report gives test counts that don't add up.

  After the fix passes re-review, I'll finish Task 3 and go on to Task 4 (readingTimeMinutes).

